WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:04.610
The Expanse is a sci-fi book series, adapted
to TV.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.889
It’s got politics, mystery, space battles,
space Mormons, and a looming alien threat

00:00:09.889 --> 00:00:13.900
– and it’s mostly based in realistic science
and technology.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.970
The Expanse is set “Hundreds of years in
the future”, when “humans have colonized

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.330
the solar system”.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:23.960
Earth is “overpopulated” and environmentally
stressed, and it’s governed by the United

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.330
Nations.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:30.500
Mars is an independent power, with advanced
technology and military, working to terraform

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.099
the red planet.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:36.890
While Earth and Mars are the big political
powers, the asteroid belt is a dangerous new

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.050
“frontier”.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:43.620
Millions of people live on Ceres, Eros, and
other rocks, mining the belt for resources.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.329
A political network called the OPA fights
for the rights of the belt against Earth and

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:49.359
Mars.

00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:54.589
Beyond the belt, Jupiter’s moons of Ganymede
and Europa grow food in greenhouses.

00:00:54.589 --> 00:00:59.440
There are resorts on Saturn’s moon Titan,
and labs on the moons of Uranus and Neptune

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.929
– “the farthest outpost[s] of human civilization”.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:07.780
Earth, Mars and the belt each have distinct
cultures and histories.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.170
Earth is controlled by the United Nations
because some time ago, Earth had a terrible

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.400
environmental “collapse”.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.290
The ice caps melted, and the sea level rose,
causing mass displacement and chaos.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:24.830
In the face of “extinction”, the nations
of Earth were forced to unite under one government.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:30.270
There are still some places resisting the
UN, but most of the planet’s under control.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:34.310
Of course, within that government there’re
factions and conflicts.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:40.050
One major character, UN politician Avasarala,
fights for peace amidst the politics.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.930
So Earth is powerful, “But it's an empire
in decline”.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:48.980
It’s way overpopulated, relying on recycling
machines to keep it from “drowning in its

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.420
own filth”.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.740
About half the planet is unemployed, living
off welfare called “basic”.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:02:00.050
Basic provides food and shelter, but no money
– and not much freedom to make your own

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.050
choices.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:05.580
So Earth feels stagnant, bureaucratic and
“bloated”, but it’s still the only place

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.979
where humans can stand beneath an open sky,
and breathe free air.

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:15.129
It’s the birthplace of humanity, and it’s
not giving up yet.

00:02:15.129 --> 00:02:18.900
Mars was settled by some of Earth’s best
scientists and engineers.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.859
They built cities underground and in domes,
developed the best spaceships and science,

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:27.700
and soon they decided they didn’t want to
serve Earth any more.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.099
Mars wanted independence, which almost caused
war with Earth.

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:36.640
But then, a Martian called Solomon Epstein
invented the Epstein drive, a rocket technology

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.579
that made spaceships fly far faster and further
than before.

00:02:40.579 --> 00:02:45.560
Solomon’s test drive accelerated so fast
that it killed him – and a hundred n thirty

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:51.170
years later, you can still see his ship shooting
into deep space – “The best, longest funeral

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.739
in … history”.

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:57.730
Mars recovered Epstein’s design, and shared
the drive with Earth in return for independence.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:02.970
So now Mars has its own government and military,
and stands as a rival superpower to Earth.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:08.719
But while Earth is bloated and slow, Mars
is driven and focussed on one goal – to

00:03:08.719 --> 00:03:13.390
terraform Mars, “to turn a lifeless rock
into a garden”.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:17.319
This shared purpose unites Martians from many
different backgrounds.

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:22.299
The Mariner Valley was settled by East Indians,
Chinese and Texans – so you get Martians

00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:26.879
like Alex Kamal, who looks Indian, but speaks
in a Texan drawl.

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:30.900
Mars brings together some of humanity’s
best and brightest with the shared goal of

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.239
transforming the red planet.

00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:37.919
But Mars’ technology and military makes
their rivalry with Earth dangerous – war

00:03:37.919 --> 00:03:41.830
could bring disaster on both planets.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.840
People born in the asteroid belt are called
Belters.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:49.529
Since they grow up in low gravity, Belters
are tall and thin, with weak bones – so

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.930
some can’t even survive the gravity of Earth.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:56.999
They’ve become a separate people, with their
own culture, adapted to space.

00:03:56.999 --> 00:04:01.689
They have their own language, and hand gestures
to communicate through spacesuits.

00:04:01.689 --> 00:04:06.439
In the show, they have special tattoos – old
spacesuits used to burn Belters’ necks,

00:04:06.439 --> 00:04:08.450
so they’d tattoo to cover the scars.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:14.109
Now, even unburned Belters get the tattoos
as marks of cultural identity.

00:04:14.109 --> 00:04:19.730
These are a people who ventured into the darkness
of space to explore, find fortune and freedom.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:24.840
But the Belt is still mostly controlled by
the inner planets – Earth and Mars.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:30.230
Inner governments and corporations own Belt
stations and mines, imposing heavy taxes,

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.590
tariffs, and unfair laws.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:38.160
Some inners are racist against Belters, seeing
them as no longer human because of their differences.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:43.410
In response to this oppression, the Outer
Planets Alliance, or OPA, fights for Belter

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.410
rights.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:49.550
But it’s a loose decentralised network that
includes criminal and terrorist elements.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:55.160
OPA leader Fred Johnson tries to unite and
legitimise the OPA – even though Fred was

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.920
originally a military leader for Earth.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.050
At the same time, Fred runs an engineering
company that’s building a giant spaceship

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:05.660
for Mormons who wanna colonise distant space.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:11.510
So The Expanse has all these different competing
factions, whose cultures and conflicts are

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.250
shaped by the physics of space.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:18.820
Like, in space, there’s almost no gravity,
which is a problem – because your muscles

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:23.060
waste away, your drinks spill everywhere,
and the VFX goes over budget.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:27.580
A lot of sci fi shows get around this by inventing
some ‘gravity plating’ that magically

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:28.770
gives ships gravity.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:34.261
But The Expanse is more realistic, cause its
spaceships use acceleration, or thrust, to

00:05:34.261 --> 00:05:35.261
make gravity.

00:05:35.261 --> 00:05:39.390
It’s like how accelerating a car pushes
you back in your seat.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:44.360
By accelerating constantly, a spaceship can
use that pushback as gravity, pulling you

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.320
down towards the thruster.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:51.890
The faster you accelerate, the stronger the
gravity – so flying at one g is Earth gravity,

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:56.550
while two g is double Earth gravity, making
you weigh twice as much.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:06:01.150
When you’re in a hurry, or in combat, ships
might fly at five or six gs.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:05.570
The Expanse has a drug called the juice which
helps people survive this – but too much

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.740
g force will kill you.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:12.630
An Epstein ship can accelerate constantly
for the first half of a trip, then flip around

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:16.890
and thrust in the other direction, to decelerate
for the rest of the trip.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:22.730
That way, it slows to a stop at the destination,
keeping thrust gravity the whole time.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.440
Real-world rockets aren’t fuel-efficient
enough to do this.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:29.440
But with the Epstein drive, the physics of
thrust gravity makes sense.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:33.900
Sometimes, though, you want gravity without
having to accelerate somewhere.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:39.440
So another method is to rotate an object so
the centrifugal force pushes you outwards.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:44.510
This looks nauseating, but from your perspective
inside the object, you’re standing still

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:46.420
– and you’ve got gravity.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:51.200
It’s like the Gravitron, that spinning carnival
ride that pushes you against the walls.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:57.000
Spin up a whole space station, and that force
is your gravity – it’s like in 2001: A

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.160
Space Odyssey.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.830
But in The Expanse, they don’t just spin
up stations.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:05.470
They take planetoids like Ceres that are too
small to have their own gravity, and they

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:09.890
artificially spin the whole rock to give it
centrifugal force.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:14.900
The spin gravity pushes outwards, so people
live on the inside of Ceres, underground.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:20.890
This spin gravity in Ceres and Eros is a third
as strong as Earth’s gravity – which causes

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:26.010
the tall thin bodies of Belters – like main
character Detective Miller.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:31.930
So the people and cultures of The Expanse
are shaped by real-world physics – and by

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.210
communication technology.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:37.350
You can’t send a message faster than the
speed of light, so it can take seconds or

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.200
minutes to send messages to distant planets.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.540
You can’t talk in real time.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:47.950
This creates tension and strategy in conflicts,
but it also has emotional impacts.

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:54.370
The comm delay separates people from those
they love, making space feel truly remote.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:58.850
Technology also changes families – main
character James Holden was born in Montana

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:04.970
to a family of three mothers and five fathers,
who each contributed to Holden’s DNA.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:11.080
Sharing one child between eight gave tax breaks
to Holden’s family on overpopulated Earth.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:14.960
So The Expanse makes some stuff up, like the
Epstein drive.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:21.060
But it also uses real science and technology
to shape its people and worlds.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:26.639
The story of The Expanse begins with Holden,
who gets into danger on an ice hauler; Detective

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:32.150
Miller, who searches for a lost girl on Ceres;
and Avasarala, who navigates UN political

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.150
intrigue.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:37.669
They’re all drawn in to a mystery and conspiracy
that threatens everything.

00:08:37.669 --> 00:08:42.280
We’re working on a video about this story
– but in the meantime, check out the first

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:44.300
book, Leviathan Wakes.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:50.460
You can get it on audiobook for free today
by signing up for a trial at audible.com/asx.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.410
Members get a free book each month, and if
you cancel, you keep the books.

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.510
Audible has all the main series Expanse books.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:02.771
So next time you’re driving, put on Leviathan
Wakes, and accelerate – to feel the gs of

00:09:02.771 --> 00:09:04.610
artificial gravity.

